# Cloudflare Pages headers for the standalone `thriftlux` project (thriftlux.pages.dev).
#
# The ThriftLux admin lives at /admin here. By default CF Pages sends no
# Cache-Control on HTML, so browsers — especially the WhatsApp/Instagram in-app
# webviews owners use — heuristically cache a stale admin.html for hours. After a
# redeploy the owner then sees an old admin (missing newly-added sections like the
# Sell-in-store receipt panel) until that cache expires. `no-cache` forces a
# revalidation on every load (304 when unchanged, fresh when redeployed) so admin
# changes show up immediately. Versioned assets (admin.js?v=, styles.css?v=) keep
# their long cache — only the HTML entry points need this.
#
# NOTE: CF only processes the `_headers` at the DEPLOY ROOT. This file is the root
# for the `thriftlux` project. The nessa project (which serves the same admin at
# /thriftlux/admin) is covered by its own root _headers; this file is ignored there.
/admin
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate
/admin.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate
